# Citation metadata: GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and Zenodo read
# this file. No version or release date on purpose: pyproject.toml is the one
# source of the version, and each release's DOI record carries its own.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Probolos, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Probolos: a deny-by-default USB admission gate for Linux"
type: software
authors:
  - name: capitan0n
    alias: capitan0n
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/capitan0n/probolos"
url: "https://github.com/capitan0n/probolos"
abstract: >-
  Probolos holds every newly attached USB device blocked through the Linux
  kernel's USB authorization interface and admits it only on a human decision,
  a remembered fingerprint, or a configured exemption. Before the decision it
  checks the device's declared identity for inconsistencies, can observe its
  input behaviour in a grabbed quarantine and read its partition metadata
  without mounting, and remembers devices across sessions to detect descriptor
  drift. The privileged half runs as a separate root gate, apart from an
  unprivileged analyzer.
keywords:
  - usb
  - security
  - badusb
  - linux
  - sysfs
  - hardening
